msgid "press ``Write Configuration`` once you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:237 f1c4928025d84d249b0684321fa47b7e
msgid ""
"Set up a new NK3 Secrets App HOTP secret by attaching the NitroKey to your "
"USB qube and running the following commands in it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:246 dbb1ac562260443099ca55b11c000170
msgid ""
"Note that the 20 digit sequence can contain any printable ASCII character, "
"e.g. letters, numbers, punctuation marks. The actual ``Secret Key (base "
"32)`` is the base32 encoded form of that sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:252 74659b6f948b45c49bbdc0bce370c716
msgid ""
"We will call the ``Secret Key (20 bytes hex)`` (YubiKey) or ``Secret Key "
"(base 32)`` ``AESKEY``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:254 7a0c133db1b440d78925fa4adfd8ed88
msgid ""
"It is recommended to keep a backup of your ``AESKEY`` in an offline VM used "
"as a vault."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:256 50fd2426eae347818e324407e0b0eea9
msgid ""
"Consider keeping a backup of your ``AESKEY`` on paper and storing it in a "
"safe place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:258 4c8d8f34ae5144888bc6f4cd447467a7
msgid ""
"If you have multiple YubiKeys for backup purposes (in case one gets lost, "
"stolen or breaks) you can write the same settings into other YubiKeys. For "
"YubiKeys you can choose “Program multiple YubiKeys” in the program; make "
"sure to select ``Same secret for all keys`` in this case. For NitroKeys you "
"can set up the secret for multiple of them, but you must always use the same "
"NitroKey, because the HOTP counter will be incremented in dom0 as well as "
"the used NitroKey whenever you make use of this method. If you want to "
"switch to a different NitroKey later, delete the file ``/etc/qubes/yk-keys/"
"nk-hotp-counter`` in dom0 first to make it work with a fresh NitroKey 3. Do "
"the same if for some reason your counters get desynchronized (it stops "
"working), e.g. due to connectivity issues (NitroKey3A Minis are known to "
"wear out quickly)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:268 5fbb2d8602ea425ca64beb35bf85a40e
msgid ""
"Paste your ``AESKEY`` into ``/etc/qubes/yk-keys/yk-secret-key.hex`` in dom0. "
"Note that if you had previously used a NitroKey3 with this package, you "
"*must* delete the file ``/etc/qubes/yk-keys/nk-hotp-secret`` or its content!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:272 caf62c4f2d9b473e9c9dafdeee2ef018
msgid ""
"Create the file ``/etc/qubes/yk-keys/nk-hotp-secret`` in dom0 and paste your "
"``AESKEY`` (in base 32 format) into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:278 b95d15fcaaff428598ec51115e82d404
msgid ""
"As mentioned before, you need to define a new password that is only used in "
"combination with the YubiKey / NitroKey3. You can write this password in "
"plain text into ``/etc/qubes/yk-keys/login-pass`` in dom0. This is "
"considered safe as dom0 is ultimately trusted anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:280 21227c9960e7478190aeaa1281e2f464
msgid ""
"However, if you prefer you can paste a hashed password instead into ``/etc/"
"qubes/yk-keys/login-pass-hashed.hex`` in dom0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:282 d7b3d58197654834a668a2f194270437
msgid ""
"You can calculate your hashed password using the following two commands. "
"First run the following command to store your password in a temporary "
"variable ``password``. (This way your password will not leak to the terminal "
"command history file.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:290 cb0b039d7f8e46cdbc9e7191daa2f2c1
msgid "Now run the following command to calculate your hashed password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:300 39f1bf8e4e2b4a9c8d20d20dfa3a1e11
msgid "To enable multi-factor authentication for a service, you need to add"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:307 64d595df491543d0b8e1d55de7853f8e
msgid ""
"(same for YubiKey and NitroKey3) to the corresponding service file in ``/etc/"
"pam.d/`` in dom0. This means, if you want to enable the login via YubiKey / "
"NitroKey3 for xfce4-screensaver (the default screen lock program), you add "
"the line at the beginning of ``/etc/pam.d/xfce4-screensaver``. If you want "
"to use the login for a tty shell, add it to ``/etc/pam.d/login``. Add it to "
"``/etc/pam.d/lightdm`` if you want to enable the login for the default "
"display manager and so on. It is important, that ``auth include yubikey`` is "
"added at the beginning of these files, otherwise it will most likely not "
"work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:310 7ee318ffa51346ceb5bf90255a17e5d4
msgid ""
"Adjust the USB VM name in case you are using something other than the "
"default ``sys-usb`` by editing ``/etc/qubes/yk-keys/vm`` in dom0."
msgstr ""

